values ('45241651-6d27-44f7-8908-f941a7418479', 'control-systems', 'Control Systems', 'Control Systems develops the analysis and design of feedback systems that remain stable, accurate, responsive, and robust in the presence of disturbances, noise, uncertainty, delays, and actuator limits. Students progress from multi-domain modeling and classical frequency-domain design to state-space control, estimation, digital implementation, robustness, optimization, nonlinear behavior, and experimental validation. One rigorous common core serves all three degrees. Electrical Engineering emphasizes circuits, motors, power, sensing, and embedded implementation, Mechanical Engineering emphasizes physical modeling, actuators, mechatronics, and experiments, and graduate students add proof, MIMO analysis, estimation, optimization, uncertainty, and research-quality design evidence.');

